00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:12.820
The Injury.
《工伤》。

237
00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:17.580
And that was a time we had a cold open on The Office that did kick off the episode.
那是我们在《办公室》里的一个冷开场，确实推动了那一集的剧情。

238
00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:22.400
That's when Michael has a George Foreman grill by his bed because he loves the fresh bacon
那是迈克尔的床边放着一个乔治·福尔曼烤架，因为他喜欢早上吃新鲜培根

239
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:23.900
in the morning and he steps on the grill.
结果他不小心踩到了烤架上。

240
00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:29.500
But so that cold open where he calls Pam in a panic is one that then leads into the
所以那个冷开场中他惊慌失措地给帕姆打电话，随后就引出了

241
00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:30.160
whole episode.
整集的故事。

242
00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.060
So we did that every once in a while.
所以我们偶尔也会这样做。

243
00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:32.620
But you're right.
不过你说得对。

244
00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.260
Mostly ours were these standalone little movies.
大部分情况下，我们的都是这种独立的小电影。

245
00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:40.900
Did you guys tell us in one of the episodes we did together that often they would write
在之前我们一起录制的一期节目中，你们是不是说过，冷开场经常会

246
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.820
it for one and it would end up on another episode?
为这一集写，结果却跑到了另一集里？

